# Core motion and reliability upgrade

Status: DONE
Milestone: VSeeFace-informed Python/GLB implementation
Dependencies: 13_BLENDER_MODEL_RUNTIME.todo, 19_VSEEFACE_RESEARCH.todo

## Purpose
Implement the first integrated motion-system upgrade while preserving truthful diagnostics,
synthetic output, the reference art, the GLB contract and the existing live-camera pause.

## Tasks
- [x] Preserve the previous verified source/receipt in a private archive.
- [x] Implement owned spawned inference, bounded request/response IPC and Windows job cleanup.
- [x] Add separately filtered world coordinates with image-based visibility gating.
- [x] Add rest-aware two-bone posing and bounded bend-plane handling.
- [x] Add display-clock rig interpolation and explicit opt-in held/returning/rest states.
- [x] Add session-only neutral/range facial calibration and per-channel response controls.
- [x] Finish UI/CLI integration and isolated debug-topology handling.
- [x] Exercise native controls, failure/cleanup behavior and the supplied recording.
- [x] Update documentation, handbook, visual evidence and current-base context.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Native tracker failures do not kill the studio; owned processes and raw previews clean up.
- [x] Rig lengths remain fixed; world coordinates are not constrained by image-coordinate bounds.
- [x] Measured diagnostics are unchanged by interpolation or inferred/rest presentation.
- [x] Whole-source staleness and total detection loss remain fail-closed.
- [x] Short blinks and independent winks survive; calibration is explicit and never written to disk.
- [x] Legacy comparison mode remains available; no claim of perfect tracking or a repaired native DLL.

